From: NeiroNext <mihail.rozshko@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:39:45 +0000
Subject: Test how the listener takes its names, per desktop

test-listener-inhibit gets listener-acquire cases on its private session
bus. Every case sets XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP; the inhibitor cases run with
XFCE. The stand-in logind records SetLockedHint, and the harness can make
the listener's request for one name fail with an error
(--wrap=dbus_bus_request_name).

 - unity_desktop_freedesktop_name_taken: another connection owns
   org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver; light-locker starts, owns
   org.gnome.ScreenSaver, the other keeps its name, one
   SetLockedHint(false).
 - other_desktop_freedesktop_name_taken: the same on XFCE; light-locker
   stops and takes no name.
 - unity_desktop_gnome_name_taken: one other connection owns both names;
   light-locker stops, both names keep their owner, no NameOwnerChanged,
   no SetLockedHint.
 - unity_desktop_freedesktop_free: light-locker owns both names.
 - unity_desktop_freedesktop_request_error: the request for
   org.freedesktop.ScreenSaver fails; light-locker starts with
   org.gnome.ScreenSaver, no error, one SetLockedHint(false).
 - unity_desktop_gnome_request_error: the request for
   org.gnome.ScreenSaver fails; light-locker stops, holds neither name,
   no SetLockedHint.

Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-17
